WEBVTT

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.670
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.960
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.520
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.770
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.370
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.680
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.960
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.090
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.960
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.940
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.710
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.140
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.650
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.880
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.080
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.680
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.920
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.300
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.230
Looks like all that
training is paying off.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.690
Master Chief!

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.300
What the hell?!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.350
<i>You okay, Master Chief?!</i>

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.470
Thanks to you!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.210
But I've never had support
fire come that close to me!

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.980
Well, now you've
seen what I can do.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.220
Where'd it come
from, Eledore?!

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.790
- <i>A pill box, top of the hill!</i>
- <i>But why's it so accurate?!</i>

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.800
- They're shooting at US!
- They can't be!

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.800
Somebody over there's
got some good ears!

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:09.640
R- Right!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.030
<i>Commander, the enemy fire's</i>
<i>hitting closer and closer!</i>

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:15.160
<i>All units! I think</i>
<i>they've got us ranged!</i>

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.310
God dammit! We're boxed in.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.670
<i>Team, scatter and fall back!</i>
<i>We'll change the plan!</i>

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:21.640
Roger!

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:30.680
Okay, three pill boxes out front...

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.690
A trench with Zakus deployed in it...

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.950
And some nasty hill
terrain for good measure.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.060
That highway, huh?

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.060
Yes, sir. That's the
most vital route...

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.160
...they have for
getting supplies in.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:47.600
For the Federal Forces, too.
We can probably make it there...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.270
...but the real problem
is that village.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.400
Yeah. We shouldn't have
let the Zeeks take it.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.380
So, how to attack pill boxes that
use the natural terrain so well?

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.150
I really wish we could call
in some support for this.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.810
If we wait for backup,
they'll hunt us down.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.220
Yeah, I know. I know, but!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.450
- What's this?
- A waterfall.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.790
If we follow the river around
to the hills on the west side...

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.030
...and then confuse them with
a sneak attack, then maybe!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.200
Easier said than done.
That area's crawling with guerrillas.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.830
Guerrillas?

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:24.470
So, who runs
the sneak attack?

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.850
I've been to the falls before, so...

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:30.960
You have, sir?

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:32.920
You'll run the sneak attack?

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.150
Hey, the commander's got
the least experience...

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.880
...so playing decoy is his
responsibility, right?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.880
Master Chief, I'm turning over
command of this group to you.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.860
- But, sir...
- No "buts." This is an order.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.190
- If you put it that way...
- Go to it!

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.530
Okay, we'll do it in...
Let's say 3 hours.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.230
I'll definitely get there within 3
hours and launch the sneak attack.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.300
When I do, you guys hit
'em from the front.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:56.850
Aye, sir!

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.870
Just to be sure you know,
I should mention that...

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.880
...we can hold out against
them for only one hour at most.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.910
I know that. Master Chief,
you four will advance...

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:09.390
...under the highway viaduct and
then stand by until 15:00 hours.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.120
When the clock hits that time,
you hit 'em as hard as you can.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:12.710
That is all!

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.320
Hope you don't get
caught by the guerrillas.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.420
The guerrillas are just
civilians, aren't they?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.490
You dumbass!

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.930
Those "civilians" are the ones
you should be most scared of!

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.630
All right! Let's get ready
to move out, too!

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.600
Right, right...

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.540
Be careful out
there, commander.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.500
It's him.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.490
Of course nobody's here.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.070
What's the big idea?!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.790
Leaving the
front line, Mr. Ensign?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.190
Apparently this little pervert didn't
learn his lesson from last time!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.920
You lucky bastard!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.590
What are you doing?!

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.270
You gotta pay the admission price
to go into the waterfall pool.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.970
You came 'cuz you thought you could
get another peep show, didn't you?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.010
Even <i>we've</i> never gotten to see that!

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.140
Cut it out!
It was an accident!

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.410
You were starin'
just by accident, huh?!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.420
Hold him down!
I'll get his stuff!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.520
- Cut it out!
- Hey! Hold still!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.020
Hey, this is new equipment.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.820
Cut it out!
What if it starts moving?!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.050
Check this out, dumbass.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.560
Stop it! Stop it, please!

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.160
Stop that!
Don't touch it! Cut it out!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.630
You're the one who's
gonna cut it out!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.110
You wanted me, didn't you?

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.410
Wh- What?

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:21.010
You soldiers are all alike!

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.050
Rude and vulgar, with dirty minds!

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:25.360
You're sure one to talk!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.950
You have no right to judge
people! First of all!

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:30.120
What?

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.230
Well, you're just a kid, right?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.460
W- Well, then! Why were
you watching me that time?!

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:41.130
Why was I? Because
you're pretty, that's all.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.200
I don't have time to waste with
you guys, so let me go, okay?

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:53.890
<i>B.B., there's been a
break in the battle.</i>

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.180
<i>For us, the tension just</i>
<i>keeps building up inside.</i>

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.620
<i>My partner Eledore won't</i>
<i>tear his ear away from...</i>

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.680
<i>...his sonar panel for even a moment</i>
<i>as he tracks the enemy's movements.</i>

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.360
<i>Right now, even I'm getting</i>
<i>ready for the next battle...</i>

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.570
Christ, how the hell'd this song
ever get to the top of the charts?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.530
Another love letter?
You sure got lots of free time!

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.440
I'm ready for
the battle, okay?!

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:20.410
I told you before, cut it
out before she dumps you!

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:21.500
- <i>Eledore!</i>
- Yeah?

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.660
- Let's go!
- <i>Roger!</i>

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:44.530
I apologized for seeing
her naked, didn't I?!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.260
Shut up and march!

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.570
I keep telling you!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.940
I don't have any time
to waste with you guys!

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.200
We're busy, too, pal.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.370
Dammit...

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.850
I don't have time for this!
Where are you taking me?!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.480
And quit poking me with that!

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:01.910
I said quit
poking me, didn't I?

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.430
Don't be rude to the
person you're gonna meet.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.900
Come on! Can't you say hello?!

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.960
God dammit...

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:29.320
Are you the boss?

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.080
What did you come to our territory
for, Ensign Shiro Amada?

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.080
Look, I'm sorry I came
in without permission!

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.930
But, right now, I'm in
the middle of a mission!

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:47.180
And?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.230
You can't have any
use for me, right?

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.300
Please, I want you
to let me go.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.570
Hey! Are you listening to me?!

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.200
Uh-oh! Look, you
gotta let me go now...

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.580
Uh... Excuse me?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:06.180
Forgive me. I always do
this at this time of the day.

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.210
Please! Listen to me seriously!

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.560
It's time. Eledore!

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.760
<i>It's quiet up above us.</i>
<i>Must be teatime for our friends.</i>

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.370
Master Chief, you think the
commander made it through okay?

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.530
<i>He seemed pretty confident</i>
<i>and sounded convincing.</i>

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:31.840
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.780
How do I explain it
so you'll understand?

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.910
The Zeon are your enemies as
well as the Federation's, right?

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.190
If we take out those guns
in that captured village...

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.020
...you guys will benefit
as well, won't you?

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.690
My friends are waiting for me
to help carry out our plan.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.200
If we liberate that
village from the Zeon...

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.860
...then your friends
there will be free!

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.910
Please! Let me go!

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.150
C'mon! Pour on the firepower!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:18.890
Commander...

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.790
Just give it up, Mr. Ensign!

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.360
Hey! Why, you!

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.300
You think you can try that
in front of our boss?!

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.130
Those people are my first command!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:39.010
I don't want to lose any
before I even get to know them!

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.270
Please, let me go!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.380
Rude, ain't he?

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:51.420
No kidding!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.120
Hey, Dad...

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.790
If we use him, we can
free the village, right?

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.100
We all have friends there.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.360
If it works, they don't have to
take orders from the Zeon anymore.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.930
Yes, that's true...

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.410
All right, I promise!
We'll free the village!

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.410
You see, Dad?

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.710
There are a lot of sick and injured
people there to take care of.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:20.250
If you need medicine, I'll get
you all you want! Just please!

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:23.050
Besides that,
we want the Zeon to suffer.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.490
You want war spoils? Fine!
You can take anything you want!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:27.960
You're not calling
the shots here, pal!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:34.460
Still... A soldier's word
isn't worth much. Right, Kiki?

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.400
I think he'll be all right.
He owes me, anyway.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.630
No kiddin'!

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.780
You don't have to
laugh all day, do you?!

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:51.740
Dad, I'll keep an eye on him.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.310
Not like you'd listen
to me if I said no.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.410
Ensign, for this one time,
I'll declare a truce between us.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.650
That was a close call for you.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.590
You should thank the girl!

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.860
Kiki, show the ensign
the way back.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.100
God dammit! There're
mud prints all over it!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:21.010
I don't have time
for this crap!

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:25.020
Dammit... It's not
like they had to beat up...

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.020
...a guy who came along
quietly with them!

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.490
Hey! If you're coming,
then get in!

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:31.580
We don't have time for this!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.720
God dammit...

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.680
Any funny business and
I'll let you have it!

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.820
And what am I gonna
try with a kid?!

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.190
I've got more
smarts than <i>you,</i> pal!

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.560
What's with you?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.570
Hey! Gimme that back!

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.170
I took it!

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.070
You can't have it!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.940
I'm just borrowing this!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.910
3:30? Only 30 minutes left!

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.910
Look, that thing just
doesn't suit you!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.210
Listen, you...

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.770
It's Kiki.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:01.950
Kiki?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.980
Kiki Rosita. You're in a
hurry, aren't you, Shiro?

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.720
Shiro?! You!
Kids should show respect...

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.420
And don't stand in front of me!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:19.270
Just hang in there...
Is there any kind of shortcut?

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.640
Following the river's
the fastest way.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.140
- Okay, we'll do that.
- But there's no path.

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:36.280
Eledore! Any movement above?

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.790
<i>Still no change!</i>

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:38.690
Commander...

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.190
How much longer?!

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.300
If they notice us, it's all over.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:49.090
I know!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.240
He's late!
Any sign of the commander yet?

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.070
<i>No, I still can't confirm it!</i>

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:03.140
- We've got company.
- What's wrong?!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.700
Be quiet!

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.810
<i>Is it the commander?</i>

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:09.820
No. Helicopters.
One... No! Two of them.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.190
They're coming back?
All units! Prep for air attack!

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:17.960
<i>Roger!</i>

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:21.120
Gimme a break!
Is this the Reaper's fault?

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.170
The Reaper?

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.530
Yeah. You!

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.270
Captain Norris, our forces
will be finishing off...

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.430
...those rats who have
crawled out into the open.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.480
Losing two Zakus is
too high a price.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:37.370
Uh, well... Please properly inform
Commandant Ginias of that later.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.380
But, of all days,
why'd they have to attack...

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.920
...on the day of the
special inspection?!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:47.320
Oh, I've heard his sister, Aina,
has grown into a very lovely woman.

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.360
Uh, excuse me, sir.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.600
God dammit!

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:56.360
This is what I get for trusting
that troublemaking commander!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:59.870
Sanders! We're played out!
Fall back to under the viaduct!

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:00.670
<i>But!</i>

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:02.070
We can't hold out any longer!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.040
<i>Master Chief!</i>

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:14.510
No doubt about it!
It's the commander!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.390
All right! Now the fun
<i>really</i> begins! Hang on tight!

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:18.950
Right!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.360
Took him long enough!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.570
The commander finishes
any job he starts!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.400
Where's it coming from?!

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.630
From over there!
They're attacking from the river!

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:37.940
A pincer move?!

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.510
Set us down now!
I'm going out in my Zaku!

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.020
I did it! I blew
their ammo dump away!

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:50.750
Are you really an ensign?

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.050
Well, excuse me!
If you want out, now's the time.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:56.420
I'll see my job as your
guide through to the end!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.390
Have it your way!

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.760
Move out! Hurry!

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.680
There! Two Zakus!

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:21.600
Right.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.000
CHARGE!!!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.370
They all came!

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.710
But there's still a
Zaku headed for them!

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.160
Come on! Forward!

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:20.210
What?! The guerrillas
are attacking, too?

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:23.010
Heh... Then it's only a
matter of time before it falls.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.910
Masado! Withdraw!
I'll buy us some time!

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.110
Right! I'll hold them
off from the north slope!

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:32.820
<i>Go to it! And I'll hit that</i>
<i>mobile suit on the west slope!</i>

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:33.820
Yes, sir!

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:49.170
Eledore!
Help those civilians out!

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.540
<i>I'm on it!</i>

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.770
All right! What's that?

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.510
Guerrillas?!

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.880
<i>Master Chief! Do you read me?</i>

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.320
Commander?

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.720
<i>Sorry I'm late!</i>
<i>Is everyone all right?</i>

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:03.780
Yeah!

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.450
<i>We're liberating the village!</i>

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.790
<i>Take special care not</i>
<i>to hurt any civilians!</i>

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:11.120
Roger!
Sanders, did you copy that?

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:12.820
Aye!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.130
No, you DON'T!

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.740
The Feddies and the guerrillas
in a joint operation?!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:36.920
Incoming!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.140
The enemy's not bad.
But we're ending this now!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:09.980
Outta the way!

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.780
Hey, I would if I could!

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:23.930
Close your eyes!

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.250
Eat this!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.660
- Did that get him?!
- I don't know.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:59.060
So, they've got a guy
who can fight underwater...

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.570
Look, there he goes!
He's getting away!

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.670
No, forget him.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:08.110
I'm in no condition to
go chasing after him.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:11.240
And we had him, too!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.380
Careful! Carry that carefully.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.390
We hit the jackpot today, guys!

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.350
They're taking everything.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:23.050
It's our right, isn't it?

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.690
Jeez, you guys are tough.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.870
What an ungrateful
bunch these guys are!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.370
What do you mean?

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.240
Well, we freed this
village, didn't we?!

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:43.210
Yeah. They could show
a little more gratitude.

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.620
Wh- What do you want?
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.390
What's the big idea?!

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:54.990
Hey! Anybody got a wrench?!

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.650
- Okay, let's rip that gun out.
- Hey! Nudie pictures!

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.730
Commander?!

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:03.490
I've arranged for transport
for the prisoners, sir.

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:06.200
- Good work.
- But, sir... This situation...

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.070
Do something
about them, please!

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:12.630
I made a promise. Let them
take whatever they want.

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.040
It doesn't really matter.
Right, Master Chief Joshua?

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:17.880
Yes, sir!
Um, just call me Karen, sir.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.550
I'm sorry I was
late today... Karen.

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:22.680
Sure.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:28.690
Shiro!

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:29.660
What?!

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:31.820
Her? She's the owner
of the watch?

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:35.260
- Huh?! No! Absolutely not!
- She is, isn't she?

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:38.460
<i>This guy actually got the</i>
<i>guerrillas to work with him...</i>

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:54.460
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:58.150
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:58.230 --> 00:23:02.290
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:02.370 --> 00:23:06.060
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:09.230
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.240
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:17.370
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:20.510
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:21.190 --> 00:23:23.650
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:28.520
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:34.390
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:38.730
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:43.630
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:47.400
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:54.540
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:58.650
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:02.720
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:06.460
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:06.530 --> 00:24:13.150
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.920
While on a mission
in the western area...

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:23.860
...Sanders demands a transfer
out of the 08th Team.

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:26.390
I've been hearing
those rumors about him...

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:29.160
...but I didn't know they
were bothering him that much.

00:24:29.230 --> 00:24:32.960
But, just then, something
terrible appears over our heads.

00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:35.200
Is this the enemy's
new secret weapon?!

00:24:35.270 --> 00:24:39.510
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:40.140 --> 00:24:41.670
"The Demon Overhead."
